WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.960
Dear Fellow Scholars, we have just

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.260
reached 250 subscribers on the channel.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.180
So far, the reception of these videos

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.520
have been overwhelmingly positive.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.920
I'll show you some of these comments on the screen in the meantime.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.019
250 subscribers. This is probably not much compared to

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.630
even mid-size YouTubers, but it means

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.359
so much to me. It means that there are

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.839
250 people, somewhere around the world

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.560
waiting for new videos to come up.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.640
This is insane! If you think about it even one subscriber is insane.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.500
Even one click from somewhere is mind-blowing!

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.340
Imagine that someone who you

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.080
have never met, somewhere on the face of earth.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.880
Perhaps in Peru.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.660
Somewhere in the United States or maybe in the middle of

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.660
Africa is excited for your work and just

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.040
waiting for you to say something.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.780
There are millions of other videos they could

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.140
watch, but they devote their time to listening to you.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.140
And now multiply this by 250.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.040
I am just sitting here in disbelief.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.780
As a computer engineer I've been working

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.350
with computers and network algorithms

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.020
for a long time but I still find this mind-blowing.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.500
I can just record the

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.250
lectures that I hold at the University

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.590
and thousands of people can watch it at

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.960
any time, even while I'm asleep at night.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.900
I can teach people while I am asleep at night!

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.920
We have over a thousand views on my

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.720
first lecture which is possibly more

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.700
people than I will ever reach through

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.720
the university seminar rows.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.280
So for all 250 of you and everyone who

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.050
has ever watched any of these videos,

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.620
thank you very much for watching and subscribing.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.090
I have created two minute

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.039
papers to show you the best of what

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:51.960
research can offer and what your

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.620
hard-earned tax money is spent on.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.640
Because that's the thing: every single

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.979
country I've been to, researchers are

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:00.810
complaining about the lack of funding,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:04.170
and rightfully so, because most of them

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.420
can't secure the funds to continue their work.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.860
But let's try to turn the argument around.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.600
Funding comes from your tax money,

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.799
and 99.9% of the case you have no idea what your

00:02:16.799 --> 00:02:19.110
money's spent on. There are lots of

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.329
incredible works published every single

00:02:21.329 --> 00:02:23.130
day of the year but the people don't

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.960
know anything about them.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.900
No one is stepping up to explain what

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.760
your money is spent on, and I am sure that

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.620
people would be happy to spend more on

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.520
research if they know what they invest in.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.720
Two Minute Papers is here to

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.860
celebrate the genius of the best and

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.600
most beautiful research results.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.840
I will be trying my best to explain all of

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.829
these works so that everyone is able to

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:44.970
understand them.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.220
It's not only for experts, it's

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.980
definitely for everyone, so thank you for

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.030
all of you

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.709
thanks for hanging in there and please,

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:55.170
spread the word. Let your friends know

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.329
about the show so even more of us can

00:02:57.329 --> 00:02:59.910
marvel at these beautiful works.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:06.769
And until then I'll see you next time!

